A demo-fitting transform can still fail on the test because demos may underdetermine which colored components are real objects versus noise. Do not assume connected-component bounding boxes define intended objects: stray cells can connect, split, or lie close to a rectangle, and bbox filling may bridge distinct structures or manufacture false filled areas.

After rejection, seek a demo that distinguishes the competing object-selection rules. Record the complete input/output difference mask, including changed and unchanged regions; identify which isolated marks disappear and which intrusions are repaired inside retained objects. Then execute the revised transform against every complete demo, checking shape and exact cell equality, before another submission. Avoid arbitrary thresholds and coordinate-specific patches unless the examples establish their general meaning.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792544811/attempts/f09a6bde40854e10915320efd39b3a55/system/state/hermes/skills/benchmarks/continual-arc-stream-solving/references/noisy-object-distractor-inference.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "continual-arc-stream-solving", "file": "references/test-clue-consistency-after-demo-fit.md", "content": "# Test-clue consistency after demo fitting

A transform can reproduce every available demonstration and still be wrong on the current test because the demos underdetermine phase, orientation, or the relation between visible clues and the completed pattern. Before submission, check the generated grid at every non-background test coordinate against the supplied color. For any task that fills or completes a pattern, these clues should generally remain unchanged and consistent. A mismatch is evidence against the candidate; do not submit just because demo fixtures pass.

After a rejection, preserve the failed output and identify the exact contradiction between the candidate and test clues. Form competing hypotheses that explain both demos and test structure, then request the next pair specifically to distinguish those hypotheses. Avoid spending submissions on a phase/orientation guess that visibly rewrites given marks. Run the actual transform on all received demo fixtures and the current test after revising, then submit only its generated output.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/ubuntu/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/runs/adhoc-hermesagentlearner-1792544811/attempts/f09a6bde40854e10915320efd39b3a55/system/state/hermes/skills/benchmarks/continual-arc-stream-solving/references/test-clue-consistency-after-demo-fit.md"}
